                            <comment id="486491" author="simmonsja" created="Tue, 3 Feb 2026 20:10:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks like you are attempting to mount with a local NID address (fd3:XXXX) that is not visible to remote nodes. This is a misconfiguration issue.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="499439" author="hornc" created="Mon, 10 Aug 2026 22:06:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I think this is a dupe of &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18041&quot; title=&quot;struct obd_uuid is too small for MGC&amp;quot;NID&amp;quot; uuid with IPv6&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-18041&quot;&gt;LU-18041&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;`lustre_start_mgc()` parses the NID correctly. There is no &quot;Can&apos;t parse NID&quot; message, and the first NID check at `obd_mount.c:322` passed. The failure is in the second loop, which counts only the NIDs that `class_add_uuid()` accepts:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;rc = class_add_uuid(nidstr, &amp;amp;nid);
if (rc == 0) ++i;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
`class_add_uuid()` rejects the NID silently:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;if (strlen(uuid) &amp;gt; UUID_MAX - 1)
        return -EOVERFLOW;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
`UUID_MAX` is 40, because `struct obd_uuid` is `char&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;40&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;`. So the limit is 39 characters. `LNET_NIDSTR_SIZE` is 64, which is why the string got this far.&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Address `fd33:3981:3213:f010:0:5254:1b:cfa4` = 34 characters.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;With `@tcp` the NID is 38 characters, so it fits. All other IPv6 mounts in that session passed.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;test_73e is the only test that uses `${NETTYPE}50`. `@tcp50` makes the NID exactly &lt;b&gt;{&lt;/b&gt;}40{&lt;b&gt;}&lt;/b&gt; characters, which is one over the limit.&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
The net number tips it over, not the address.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
